{
  "message": "I've checked the goal against your hours: start with one island and defer co-op. Since the founder joined after the unverified sprint, don't assume earlier work is ready. Before approving, add the build and testing tasks below so we can check progress against something playable. See you at the first sprint review; I look forward to your builds and devlog posts ;)",
  "tasks": [],
  "add": [
    "By the end of week one, make a rough sailing prototype on one island and share a playable build.",
    "By the end of week two, add a tide cycle that changes where the boat can sail and share the updated build.",
    "During weeks three and four, have five players try the prototype and record where sailing or tides confused them in a shared test report."
  ],
  "goal": {
    "fit": "narrow",
    "note": "Without a shown build, two islands and co-op put testing at risk within 40–60 hours; this is common and fixable within this checkpoint. Use this goal: A rough, playable one-island sailing prototype with a working tide loop, tested by five players, with findings recorded.",
    "stage": {
      "inside": true,
      "note": ""
    }
  }
}

